From: arch-xiaomi-sheng maintainers <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] soundwire: qcom: handle wake runtime-PM errors as IRQs

An irqreturn_t handler must not return a negative errno.  When runtime resume
fails, returning that errno is interpreted as IRQ_NONE.  A level-high wake
line then reaches the spurious interrupt threshold and the IRQ core disables
the SoundWire wake interrupt permanently.

Disable the asserted wake IRQ on the error path, as the successful runtime
resume path does, and report the interrupt handled.  Runtime suspend will
re-enable the wake IRQ after the device has recovered.

Signed-off-by: arch-xiaomi-sheng maintainers <noreply@example.invalid>
---
 drivers/soundwire/qcom.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/soundwire/qcom.c b/drivers/soundwire/qcom.c
index d3d3808d21ec..ab3d282d7846 100644
--- a/drivers/soundwire/qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/soundwire/qcom.c
@@ -699,6 +699,10 @@ static irqreturn_t qcom_swrm_wake_irq_handler(int irq, void *dev_id)
 				    __func__, ret);
 		pm_runtime_put_noidle(ctrl->dev);
-		return ret;
+		if (ctrl->wake_irq > 0 &&
+		    !irqd_irq_disabled(irq_get_irq_data(ctrl->wake_irq)))
+			disable_irq_nosync(ctrl->wake_irq);
+
+		return IRQ_HANDLED;
 	}
 
 	if (ctrl->wake_irq > 0) {
-- 
